{
  "_README": [
    "PLANT CLOSURE CALENDAR, rule G3. Read by planner/cmbc/holiday.py via",
    "planner.paths.holidays(month). RENAME THIS FILE TO holidays_2026-08.json",
    "TO ARM IT -- while it ends in .example nothing opens it, and the engine is",
    "byte-identical to a run with no calendar at all.",
    "",
    "A holiday is a PLANT-DAY, 07:00 -> 07:00. '2026-08-15' therefore closes",
    "[2026-08-15 07:00, 2026-08-16 07:00): no press cures and no machine builds",
    "in that window. Work is not lost -- a cure campaign that meets the closure",
    "PAUSES and resumes, a build run is finished before the plant shuts.",
    "",
    "Two accepted shapes:",
    "  a bare list          [\"2026-08-15\"]              closes BOTH plants",
    "  an object            {\"all\": [...],              closes both",
    "                        \"PCR\": [...],              PCR only",
    "                        \"TBR\": [...]}              TBR only",
    "",
    "For an A/B arm use the env var instead -- it takes priority over this file:",
    "  PLANNER_HOLIDAYS=2026-08-15",
    "  PLANNER_HOLIDAYS=PCR:2026-08-15,TBR:2026-08-16",
    "  PLANNER_HOLIDAYS=            (set but empty = explicitly NO holidays,",
    "                                suppresses this file so an arm can prove",
    "                                the negative)",
    "",
    "BEFORE ARMING THIS ON A NEW MONTH, CHECK R5. A closed day spends shelf",
    "life: August 2026 went from 64.2 h to 69.0 h of max GT wait on PCR against",
    "a HARD 72 h limit. Two consecutive closed days, or one in a tighter month,",
    "will breach it, and R5 volume is LOST rather than delayed. The measurement",
    "is in planner/cmbc/holiday.py and PARTITION_AND_CHANGEOVER.md 4aa."
  ],
  "all": ["2026-08-15"]
}
